  %% Tightened: flow-tighten 2026-11-02 (second pass), rules 22 (start and the agent wait are two commands, so two pinned exec steps; no provider-power child for Incus), 16 (no read before the start: a VM that already runs counts as started, and the agent wait proves it), 9 (one read of the agent and the Pi, one native `assert`), 14 (no `result` print; the Gateway reads the step statuses, and the recorded host key pin stays), 15 (no `eligible` assert: the Gateway refuses an ineligible VM at dispatch), 2 (resume no longer runs the SSH preparation child; package and host keys stay with provision).
  %% status: draft
  %% command: none · a workspace operation wakes the VM
  %% kind: task_vm.resume
  autonumber
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane H icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  %% lane VM icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant H as Task VM host<br/>Node 13 over ssh
  participant VM as Task VM<br/>tvm-333 over ssh
  Note over GW: Validate, record the task<br/>task VM 333 · task #5181 · Node 13
  %%> Started by:
  %%> - `WakeTaskVmAction`, when a workspace operation needs parked VM 333 or finds a `ready` VM stopped
  %%> - the operator command `task-vms:resume 333` on the Gateway; there is no orbit CLI command
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - task VM 333 is `parked`, or `ready` for a convergence; its guest Node has a recorded host key
  %%> - no other task holds `task_vm:333`; a repeated admission returns the same open task
  %%> Result:
  %%> - task #5181 records the host, the VM, guest Node 340, its recorded host key pin and mode `resume` or `converge`
  %%> - clears the stop proof
  Note over GW: open: Nick decides<br/>converge as its own kind?
  %%> Why:
  %%> - convergence of a running VM shares this kind today; it is not a resume
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-task-vm-resume
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - starts one Swamp run on serve (Node 209)
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - the intent and `execution_secrets` as vault key names
  %%> - the Gateway refuses a VM that left its admitted state at dispatch; no `eligible` assert re-checks it (rule 15)
    SW->>H: Start the VM<br/>ssh exec · incus start
    %%> How:
    %%> - one pinned `@swamp/ssh exec` argv: `sudo timeout 60 incus start --project orbit-tasks -- tvm-333`
    %%> - a VM that already runs counts as started; the next step proves it (rule 16)
    SW->>H: Wait for the guest agent<br/>ssh exec · incus wait
    %%> How:
    %%> - `sudo timeout 130 incus wait --project orbit-tasks tvm-333 agent --timeout 120`: Incus's own bounded wait
  opt VM was ready (converge)
    SW->>VM: Converge 209 SSH access<br/>ssh exec · forEach of 3
    %%> When:
    %%> - mode `converge`; a parked VM kept its SSH access on its disk, so a resume skips this (rule 1)
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - one exec each, through `incus exec` on the host: 209's authorized key, the TCP 22 rule for 209 and `sshd`
  end
  SW->>VM: Read the guest state<br/>ssh exec · forEach of 2
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - two pinned execs over WireGuard with the recorded host key: `systemctl is-active orbit-agent`, and the Pi capabilities with the Pi token file
  %%> Not included:
  %%> - the Pi build digest check: the parked disk holds the build that provision proved (rule 1)
  SW->>SW: Check the guest is ready<br/>assert
  %%> End check:
  %%> - a native `assert`: the agent is `active` and the Pi answered
  alt every step passes
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>tvm-333 ready
    %%> How the Gateway learns it:
    %%> - its run reader sees the terminal event and reads the run once
    %%> Result:
    %%> - task VM 333 is `ready`; the waiting workspace operation goes on
    %%> - task #5181 succeeds
  else a step fails
    VM--xSW: exit ≠ 0 or timeout
    %%> When:
    %%> - the VM does not start within 120 seconds, or the agent or Pi does not answer
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>resume_failed, failed step
    %%> Result:
    %%> - task #5181 fails with `task_vm.resume_failed`; a parked VM 333 becomes `failed` with the error
    %%> On the Node:
    %%> - the VM may stay running; there is no rollback
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - a failed VM stays final; the group asks for assistance, and `task:cancel` destroys the VM
  end
